# Copy this file to .env and adjust as needed
# SQLite file database (folder db/ is git-ignored, created on first run)
DATABASE_URL="file:./db/custom.db"

# ── Telegram (the ONLY place to configure notifications) ────────────────────
# Fill both lines below and the bot + channel will work after a restart.
# To change token/channel: edit these two lines (or run deploy/set-telegram-env.sh) + restart.
#   • TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN: token from @BotFather (form 123456789:AAE…)
#   • TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID:   channel id (-100…) OR public link/name —
#       https://t.me/airealtime, @airealtime, airealtime are all accepted
#       (the app normalises them to @airealtime). Private channels must use
#       the numeric -100… id: add the bot as channel admin then fetch the id
#       via Telegram Bot API (getUpdates / getChat).
#   • TELEGRAM_API_BASE:  ALWAYS leave empty unless you really run a Bot API
#       proxy (Cloudflare Worker — see DEPLOY.md §6). Never put localhost:3000
#       here (that makes the app call itself → "fetch failed"; newer builds
#       ignore that value automatically).
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
TELEGRAM_API_BASE=
